{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899","id":"pg_1f13b2f7019153c78f8e9fe5cab1e659","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gabrielmaialva33-winx-code-agent-readme-pt-md-a48e7a9f7e86-9fe5cab1e659.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_626945a575e6511e95cda9fbe2f34c98"],"title":"gabrielmaialva33/winx-code-agent/README.pt.md @ a48e7a9f7e86","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899","id":"pg_5e88b39991495444ab50eaffb8bbeb2f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gabrielmaialva33-winx-code-agent-code-of-conduct-md-a48e7a9f7e86-eaffb8bbeb2f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_853b5ddc3f9a5cb3a09127cad044e07e"],"title":"gabrielmaialva33/winx-code-agent/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md @ a48e7a9f7e86","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0c44421c9e3214370ff6ae51fa9e18ea24e9810789938d65cee3b1a07512b48d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Durable sessions survive HTTP disconnects: guardians are capped at 32 by default with tiered idle retention (30 minutes never-used, 24 hours used), and active commands are never evicted."},{"claim_ids":["clm_11ff99f9eb38a7e680c02a6444ea1f3dae14710abfec58990717c078d122ee6b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The SEARCH/REPLACE matcher tolerates model mistakes: indentation adjustment, smart-quote normalization, line-number stripping, neighbor-block disambiguation, and one retry on over-escaped quotes, while refusing heavily fuzzy matches."},{"claim_ids":["clm_13bd3a346b30c7b50bf5512510615d7a0bb26734cea32f4b292e980193f8b699"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"HTTP security defaults include loopback-only binding, 32-byte minimum bearer tokens, chmod-600 token files, DNS-rebinding host checks, 64 MiB body cap, 120 req/min per-IP rate limiting, and delayed invalid-auth responses."},{"claim_ids":["clm_498d289ab333b26845e9bea1a7442bd09115936d7e574d82a70753ff9058492c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README warns that a valid principal is equivalent to shell and file access as the OS user, and that BashCommand in wcgw mode is not workspace-confined."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6d461971413b29e13aa6de780592d6e79d453b1308a861ac4eacf1169117ac81"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On Unix, the MCP adapter is separated from PTY-owning processes: winxd manages the control plane and one winx-guardian per session keeps shells alive across disconnects and adapter upgrades."},{"claim_ids":["clm_be9e773f1613dfe0ba8f4a425042b68bc83be5f11c0ae3fcba71ea2e1d0128ab"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Winx advertises MCP 2026-07-28; every tool publishes an outputSchema and returns a structuredContent envelope whose authoritative status field enumerates states like completed, conflict, needs_read, and denied."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c76755fb1b3d5d067bce1993547f1583eb8a2554b909a991373d96dee48dbb01"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The single mutation tool EditFiles supports replace, SEARCH/REPLACE, revision-bound line patches, atomic batches, verification, and undo, with legacy edit names kept as hidden compatibility aliases."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c8e4d665c37d330a8a24ba66bf52949e3d865968f2595414dd4a8a11446a144e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workspaces have three modes: wcgw (full access), architect (read-only), and code_writer (command allowlist plus write globs), with the allowlist parsed via tree-sitter to check every command including pipelines and substitutions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ca797917cdac719391d5d6289ae7a93bf16460945d5ba98c6eb1925691caa934"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MCP Tasks on BashCommand are capability-driven: adaptive promotes only after runtime state is running, until_complete creates a Task immediately, and return_early never does; cancellation is generation-bound with a fail-closed fallback."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d90c1e8ff044aa2a9a6b34cbda42fc588922e04af9c4a8ec87dcddba1b1134a2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Winx is a remote-first MCP runtime exposing a Streamable HTTP endpoint at /mcp (default 127.0.0.1:8000) plus a stdio transport for local clients like Claude Code, Cursor, and VS Code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dd2cba8dbd10a6a67da84f4938f0cda1e96b2ac009fe6ba4aba5a595464a10a8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Building requires Rust 1.88+ and bash; the durable daemon runtime is supported on Linux/macOS/WSL2, while native Windows uses an embedded runtime with sessions tied to the server process."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed8671aa6e67eae8708539aaf717048ad72fa9b209551d701e557448b1f64aba"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tool catalogs are profiled as terminal (2 tools), read-only (4), coding (5), and full (7), or an exact per-principal allowlist; policy is enforced at both discovery and dispatch."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0c44421c9e3214370ff6ae51fa9e18ea24e9810789938d65cee3b1a07512b48d","clm_11ff99f9eb38a7e680c02a6444ea1f3dae14710abfec58990717c078d122ee6b","clm_13bd3a346b30c7b50bf5512510615d7a0bb26734cea32f4b292e980193f8b699","clm_498d289ab333b26845e9bea1a7442bd09115936d7e574d82a70753ff9058492c","clm_6d461971413b29e13aa6de780592d6e79d453b1308a861ac4eacf1169117ac81","clm_be9e773f1613dfe0ba8f4a425042b68bc83be5f11c0ae3fcba71ea2e1d0128ab","clm_c76755fb1b3d5d067bce1993547f1583eb8a2554b909a991373d96dee48dbb01","clm_c8e4d665c37d330a8a24ba66bf52949e3d865968f2595414dd4a8a11446a144e","clm_ca797917cdac719391d5d6289ae7a93bf16460945d5ba98c6eb1925691caa934","clm_d90c1e8ff044aa2a9a6b34cbda42fc588922e04af9c4a8ec87dcddba1b1134a2","clm_dd2cba8dbd10a6a67da84f4938f0cda1e96b2ac009fe6ba4aba5a595464a10a8","clm_ed8671aa6e67eae8708539aaf717048ad72fa9b209551d701e557448b1f64aba"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","created_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899","id":"pg_663106d9bcc95c1fa3a6dedaac2578fa","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/gabrielmaialva33-winx-code-agent-readme-md-a48e7a9f7e86-dedaac2578fa.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_6ce5b3301cc853339f515f7626188d8c"],"title":"gabrielmaialva33/winx-code-agent/README.md @ a48e7a9f7e86","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:52:35Z","updated_by_operation":"op_bb941566565546969d278ba2daf94899"}
